---
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Do ip4 ranges count toward the limit?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "No. ip4 and ip6 are answered from the record itself and cost zero lookups. Only include, a, mx, ptr, exists, and redirect consume the budget." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "What happens exactly at 11 lookups?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Evaluation stops and receivers return permerror: the record stops protecting the domain, and mail may fail authentication." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Does the checker follow nested includes?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Our checker counts the top-level terms in your record and warns about nested includes, which consume additional lookups during real evaluation." } }
  ],
};
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import ToolPanel from '../components/ToolPanel.astro';

---
<BaseLayout
  schema={[faqSchema]}
  title="The SPF 10-Lookup Limit Explained (and How to Stay Under It)"
  description="The SPF 10-DNS-lookup limit explained: what counts as a lookup, why exceeding it causes permerror, and three ways to fix it."
  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["Email Authentication", "/email-authentication/"], ["SPF Lookup Limit"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">SPF Lookup Limit</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">SPF Lookup Limit Auditor: Count DNS-Querying Mechanisms</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      SPF evaluation is deliberately capped: receivers will follow at most <strong class="text-ink">10 DNS
      lookups</strong> per record. Cross that line and your SPF doesn't get stricter, it stops working
      entirely, returning <code class="font-mono text-accent-soft">permerror</code>.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Lookup cost per mechanism</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Mechanism</th><th>Lookups</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">include</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">1 + nested</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">a / mx</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">1</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">ptr</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">1 (deprecated)</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">exists</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">1</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">ip4 / ip6 / all</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">0</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#what-counts-as-a-lookup">What counts as a lookup</a></li>
        <li><a href="#why-the-limit-exists">Why the limit exists</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-three-fixes">The three fixes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#check-where-you-stand">Check where you stand</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <Diagram name="spf-eval" caption="SPF evaluation: first match wins, lookup counting" />

    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 id="what-counts-as-a-lookup">What counts as a lookup</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>include:</code> each one, and each nested include inside it</li>
        <li><code>a</code> and <code>mx</code> mechanisms (with or without a domain)</li>
        <li><code>exists:</code></li>
        <li><code>redirect=</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        What doesn't count: <code>ip4:</code> and <code>ip6:</code> (no DNS involved), <code>all</code>,
        and <code>exp=</code>. A typical Google Workspace + one ESP record starts at 2-3 lookups; add a
        helpdesk, a CRM, and a billing system and you can hit 10 before noticing.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why-the-limit-exists">Why the limit exists</h2>
      <p>
        Every lookup is a DNS query a receiver must make, per message, before it can even score your
        mail. Without a cap, a single crafted record could turn every inbound email into a DNS
        amplification attack. The cap is a DoS protection, and it's enforced strictly.
      </p>

      <h2 id="the-three-fixes">The three fixes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Remove dead includes.</strong> Every service you stopped using is still spending lookups. Audit first.</li>
        <li><strong>Flatten.</strong> Replace includes with their IP ranges: zero lookups, at the cost of tracking upstream changes. Our <a href="/spf-flattener/">free flattener</a> does this automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Use SPF on fewer subdomains</strong> and keep separate records per sending domain instead of one mega-record.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="check-where-you-stand">Check where you stand</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/spf-record-checker/">SPF checker</a> counts your lookups with a live meter. If
        you're above 8, flatten before the next SaaS you add tips you over.
      </p>

      
<h2 id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/spf-record/">SPF: the complete guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/spf-flattener/">SPF Flattener (free)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do ip4 ranges count toward the limit?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. ip4 and ip6 are answered from the record itself and cost zero lookups. Only include, a, mx, ptr, exists, and redirect consume the budget.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens exactly at 11 lookups?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Evaluation stops and receivers return permerror: the record stops protecting the domain, and mail may fail authentication.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does the checker follow nested includes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Our checker counts the top-level terms in your record and warns about nested includes, which consume additional lookups during real evaluation.</p></details></div>
      </div>
</BaseLayout>
